To set up BGP for automatic path switching on IPv6 label-based forwarding during link failures in your 6PE environment, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 2 receive
    exit
    backup-path label-ipv6
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `label-ipv6 send 2 receive` enables BGP Add-Paths to advertise and receive multiple labeled IPv6 routes (up to 2 paths per prefix), providing redundancy.  
- `backup-path label-ipv6` activates BGP fast reroute for labeled IPv6 traffic, ensuring rapid failover to precomputed backup paths during link failures.  

This configuration minimizes downtime without relying on bandwidth signaling.
