To configure your BGP neighbor groups for handling unexpected error messages during graceful restarts, apply these commands within your BGP group configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp group "CLUSTER_GROUP"
    graceful-restart
    error-handling
        update-fault-tolerance
    exit
```

### Key actions:
1. **`graceful-restart`**  
   Enables helper functionality to maintain sessions during neighbor reboots.

2. **`update-fault-tolerance`**  
   Processes malformed UPDATE messages non-disruptively (treats errors as withdrawals rather than session resets).

Replace `"CLUSTER_GROUP"` with your actual BGP group name. These settings ensure neighbors continue processing routes during restarts and error conditions.
