To configure BGP to prefer paths with the lowest total internal cost across your network and external partners, enable the AIGP attribute on the relevant BGP peers. This ensures path selection uses end-to-end IGP metrics, including partner networks.

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "EXTERNAL_PARTNERS"
            aigp
        exit
    exit
```

**Key details:**  
- Apply this configuration to BGP groups/neighbors peering with external partners.  
- AIGP must be supported by partner routers to propagate the accumulated metric.  
- Paths with the lowest AIGP metric are prioritized during BGP best-path selection.  

