```cli
configure router bgp
    group "LEGACY_GROUP"
        neighbor <legacy_neighbor_IP>
            def-recv-evpn-encap vxlan
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `def-recv-evpn-encap vxlan` forces the router to treat EVPN routes without the BGP encapsulation attribute as VXLAN-encapsulated.  
- Replace `"LEGACY_GROUP"` with your BGP group name and `<legacy_neighbor_IP>` with the IP of the non-compliant neighbor.  
- Apply this at the neighbor/group level where legacy devices send routes to avoid impacting other sessions.
