To enable BGP neighbors to receive alternate outbound paths for labeled IPv6 routes while preserving the primary forwarding path, configure the add-paths capability for labeled-unicast IPv6:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group_name>
        add-paths
            label-ipv6 send 2
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group_name>` with your BGP group name. The `send 2` parameter advertises the best path plus one alternate path (e.g., second-best) for labeled IPv6 prefixes. Primary forwarding remains unchanged as the router continues using the best path locally.

For neighbor-specific configuration instead of group-level:
```cli
configure router bgp
    neighbor <neighbor_ip>
        add-paths
            label-ipv6 send 2
        exit
    exit
```
