To make BGP sessions more resilient to brief link flaps on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following configuration to disable immediate session teardown and enforce a hold-time wait:

```cli
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `disable-fast-external-failover` prevents BGP from instantly tearing down sessions when a physical link blip occurs. Instead, BGP will wait for the negotiated hold-time (default 90 seconds) to expire before declaring the session down, allowing brief interruptions to recover without resetting peerings.  

Apply this globally under the BGP context to affect all peers, or target specific groups/neighbors if needed. No other hold-time adjustments are required unless you need to modify failure detection timing.
