To ensure BGP on your Nokia 7750 SR honors and processes the additional path capacity information (e.g., link-bandwidth extended communities) attached to IPv4 routes from external neighbors, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "EBGP_GROUP"  # Replace with your eBGP group name
        link-bandwidth
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key Points:
1. **`aggregate-used-paths`** enables BGP to aggregate bandwidth metrics from the link-bandwidth extended communities of multipaths used for IPv4 routes. This ensures the router processes and honors the additional path capacity data when readvertising routes with `next-hop-self`.
