To address the BGP route flapping on your Nokia 7750 SR routers while ensuring stable routes converge quickly, configure **BGP route damping** with a tuned policy. This suppresses unstable routes without delaying stable route convergence:

```cli
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement "BGP_DAMPING"
            entry 10
                action accept
                    damping half-life 10 reuse 1500 suppress 3000 max-suppress 30
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        damping
        import "BGP_DAMPING"
    exit
```

**Key details:**
- The policy `BGP_DAMPING` applies moderate damping parameters:
  - **`half-life 10`**: Penalty halves every 10 minutes (faster clearance than default 15).
  - **`reuse 1500`**: Routes unsuppressed when penalty drops below 1500 (higher than default 750).
  - **`suppress 3000`**: Routes suppressed only if penalty exceeds 3000 (higher than default 2000).
  - **`max-suppress 30`**: Maximum suppression time capped at 30 minutes (shorter than default 60).
- Enabling `damping` in BGP activates the feature, while the `import` policy applies damping to incoming routes.

**Why this works:**  
Damping selectively penalizes flapping routes, suppressing them temporarily while allowing stable routes to converge normally. The tuned parameters ensure only severely unstable routes are suppressed, with shorter penalty durations to avoid over-penalizing marginally unstable paths.
