To address flapping prefixes while maintaining fast convergence for stable routes, enable BGP route damping. This suppresses unstable routes without impacting stable route convergence. Here's the configuration:

```
configure router policy-options
    dampening "flap-control" half-life 15 reuse 750 suppress 2000 max-suppress 60
    policy-statement "damp-policy"
        entry 10
            action accept
                damping "flap-control"
            exit
        exit
    exit
configure router bgp
    damping
    import "damp-policy"
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- The `dampening` profile defines thresholds (adjust values based on your network):  
  - `half-life 15`: Penalty halves every 15 minutes  
  - `reuse 750`: Re-advertise routes when penalty drops below 750  
  - `suppress 2000`: Suppress routes when penalty exceeds 2000  
  - `max-suppress 60`: Maximum suppression time of 60 minutes  
- The `import "damp-policy"` applies damping to received routes  
- `damping` enables the feature globally (can also apply per-group/neighbor)  

Adjust suppression thresholds based on observed flap patterns. Stable routes bypass damping and converge normally.
