The requirement is to prevent external dynamic paths (BGP routes) from being installed in the main routing table and hardware forwarding while still being received and processed. This is achieved using BGP import policies to reject route installation.

Create and apply an import policy:
```
configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement REJECT-ROUTES
    entry 10
        from protocol bgp
        action reject
    exit
commit
exit
```

Apply the policy to BGP groups or neighbors:
```
configure router bgp
group "EBGP"
    import REJECT-ROUTES
exit
exit
```

This policy matches all BGP routes and rejects them from being installed in the routing table, but they remain in the BGP RIB-IN for processing. Adjust the group name ("EBGP") to match your BGP peer configuration.
