To adjust BGP path processing for traffic balancing using "capacity-tagged" route attributes like link size metadata, configure BGP best-path selection to recognize and act on MED values (which can carry capacity metadata). Use the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        always-compare-med zero
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `always-compare-med` forces BGP to compare MED attributes across all paths (even from different ASes).  
- `zero` treats routes without MED values as having a MED of 0 (preferring lower values).  

Apply this under `config>router>bgp>best-path-selection` to globally influence path selection. To use capacity tags, ensure your route policies set MED values based on the "capacity-tagged" attributes during route import/export.
