To configure BGP on your Nokia 7750 SR to handle next-hop information for IPv4 routes with MPLS labels using a tunnel setup, apply the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family vpn-ipv4
                    resolution any
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
    group <group-name>
        next-hop-self
    exit
```

**Explanation:**
- `enable-rr-vpn-forwarding` imports VPN-IP routes into a dummy VRF for next-hop resolution via tunnels.
- Under `next-hop-resolution`, `transport-tunnel` configures tunnel options for labeled routes. The `family vpn-ipv4` scope targets IPv4 routes with MPLS labels.
- `resolution any` allows next-hop resolution using any supported tunnel type (prioritized by TTM).
- `next-hop-self` in the BGP group context ensures the local router's address is used as the next-hop when advertising routes (required when modifying next-hop information).

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP peer group name. This setup ensures VPN-IPv4 routes resolve next-hops via tunnels and re-advertise with updated labels.
