To configure your Nokia 7750 SR to only send BGP routes with link-bandwidth extended communities to a specific neighbor, apply the following CLI commands. This enables extended community-based outbound route filtering and ensures link-bandwidth communities are included for EBGP peers.

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            outbound-route-filtering
                extended-community
            exit
            link-bandwidth
                send-to-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`outbound-route-filtering`**: Enables extended community-based filtering for the BGP neighbor.
2. **`extended-community`**: Specifies that the filtering should check for extended community attributes (like link-bandwidth).
3. **`link-bandwidth` + `send-to-ebgp ipv4`**: Ensures IPv4 routes include the link-bandwidth extended community when advertised to EBGP peers. Replace `ipv4` with other address families (e.g., `ipv6`) if needed.

### Notes:
- Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your BGP group name and neighbor IP address.
- This configuration relies on the peer supporting extended community ORF negotiation. Routes without the link-bandwidth community will be filtered out.
