To ensure only one type of BGP path (either MPLS-tagged or regular IPv4) is kept in the routing and forwarding tables, adjust the BGP next-hop resolution filters. Use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnels
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter none
        exit
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter [select one or more tunnel types, e.g., rsvp]
```

### Explanation:
- **For regular IPv4 paths (unlabeled)**:  
  Disable resolution via tunnels by setting `resolution-filter none` under `shortcut-tunnels family ipv4`. This ensures only non-tunneled (IGP) paths are used for regular IPv4 routes.

- **For MPLS-tagged paths (labeled)**:  
  Specify which tunnel types (e.g., `rsvp`, `sr-policy`) are allowed to resolve labeled routes under `labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv4`. Only these tunnel types will be used for MPLS-tagged paths.

This configuration prevents both path types from cluttering the tables by selectively enabling resolution for one type and disabling it for the other. Adjust the tunnel types (e.g., `rsvp`, `sr-policy`) in the `labeled-routes` section based on your preferred tunneling mechanism.
