To configure the BGP neighbor while hiding your real ASN details in advertised routes:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            local-as 64512 private no-prepend-global-as
```

**Key points:**
1. Uses a placeholder AS (64512) instead of your real AS 65535 in routes sent to the peer
2. `private` hides the placeholder AS in routes *received* from the peer
3. `no-prepend-global-as` removes your real AS 65535 from routes *sent* to the peer
4. Replace `<peer-group-name>` and `<peer-ip-address>` with your actual values

This configuration ensures the peer only sees the placeholder AS (64512) in path advertisements, completely hiding your real ASN (65535) and backbone AS details.
