To restrict traffic for plain BGP destinations to only use RSVP-TE paths or IS-IS SR-based LSPs on a Nokia 7750 SR, configure the BGP next-hop resolution filter for unlabeled routes:

```console
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunn
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter rsvp sr-isis
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter rsvp sr-isis
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
This configuration explicitly permits only two tunnel types for BGP next-hop resolution of unlabeled routes:
1. **`rsvp`**: RSVP-TE LSPs  
2. **`sr-isis`**: Segment Routing tunnels created by IS-IS  

All other tunnel types (e.g., LDP, static, or SR tunnels from other protocols) are excluded from path consideration for plain BGP destinations.
