To configure your Nokia 7750 SR to announce the default route (0.0.0.0/0) only to specific BGP neighbors, use the following CLI commands. This setup creates a policy to match the default route and applies it as an export policy to the selected neighbors.

```cli
/configure router policy-options
    prefix-list DEFAULT_ROUTE
        prefix 0.0.0.0/0 exact
    exit
    policy-statement EXPORT_DEFAULT
        entry 10
            from
                prefix-list "DEFAULT_ROUTE"
            exit
            action accept
        exit
    exit
exit
/configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-IP>
    export "EXPORT_DEFAULT"
exit
```

**Replace placeholders**:
- `<group-name>`: Name of the BGP group containing the target neighbors.
- `<neighbor-IP>`: IP address of each neighbor that should receive the default route.

**Notes**:
1. Repeat the neighbor configuration block for each specific neighbor.
2. This policy **overrides** any existing export policy for these neighbors. If you need to retain other route advertisements, chain the policies:
   ```cli
   /configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-IP>
       export "EXPORT_DEFAULT" "<existing-export-policy>"
   exit
   ```
