To address the issue of BGP route flapping due to IGP metric changes during best-path selection when multiple identical paths exist, configure BGP multipath to install equivalent paths and avoid IGP metric-based tie-breaking:

```cli
configure router bgp
    multipath 8 restrict exact-as-path
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `multipath 8` enables ECMP for up to 8 identical paths.
- `restrict exact-as-path` ensures only paths with identical AS paths are considered equivalent, bypassing IGP metric (step 9) and router ID (step 10) comparisons.
- This configuration stabilizes forwarding by installing all qualifying paths simultaneously, eliminating flapping caused by IGP metric fluctuations. Adjust the value `8` to match your maximum path requirements.
