To dynamically filter IP ranges shared or blocked in BGP routing updates without manual access list updates, enable Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) at the BGP group level. This allows the router to exchange dynamic filter lists with peers. Use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        outbound-route-filtering
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
- Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP peer group name.
- ORF automatically negotiates and applies prefix-based filters between BGP peers.
- Filters are dynamically updated via BGP messages—no manual access list changes are needed.
- ORF applies to all neighbors in the specified group.

For extended community-based filtering (e.g., route-targets), add this under ORF:
```cli
    outbound-route-filtering
        extended-community
    exit
``` 

To accept dynamic BGP sessions from neighbors (optional):
```cli
    dynamic-neighbor
        prefix <ip-prefix/prefix-length>
    exit
    dynamic-neighbor-limit <peers>
```
Replace `<ip-prefix/prefix-length>` with the allowed neighbor subnet (e.g., `192.0.2.0/24`) and `<peers>` with the maximum sessions (1-8192).
