To configure the desired staggered path recalculation timers on your 7750 SR for BGP session flaps, use the `damp-peer-oscillations` command with the specified parameters:

```cli
configure router bgp
    damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 1 1 2
```

**Explanation:**  
- `idle-hold-time 1` (initial-wait): Sets the first session hold time to **1 minute** (meets the "at least 10 seconds" requirement, rounded to the nearest minute).  
- `1` (second-wait): Configures the second session hold time to **1 minute** (meets the "30 seconds before the next check" minimum, rounded to the nearest minute). This value doubles after subsequent failures within the error interval.  
- `2` (max-wait): Caps the maximum hold time between recalculations at **2 minutes** (prevents longer delays during continuous bouncing).  

This configuration ensures exponential backoff starting from 1 minute, doubling after repeated failures (1 min → 2 min), while never exceeding the 2-minute ceiling. Apply it globally under `config>router>bgp` for system-wide behavior.
